{"items":[{"tags":["reactjs","syntaxhighlighter"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":69528005,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1688404612,"creation_date":1633962939,"body":"I&#39;m trying to pass a string of markup into the highlighter but its only displaying it on a single line. I want it to look exactly like the markup I&#39;m passing in.\nHow I&#39;m passing the string into the child component\n\nThe code block that renders the highlighter\n\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m trying to pass a string of markup into the highlighter but its only displaying it on a single line. I want it to look exactly like the markup I&#39;m passing in.\nHow I&#39;m passing the string into the ch &hellip; ","title":"How to make React SyntaxHighlighter display multiple lines"},{"tags":["javascript","syntax-highlighting"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":76584763,"is_answered":false,"question_id":76566400,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1688080074,"creation_date":1688074955,"body":"I can guess that it must be extremely hard to calculate the same caret position in highlighted content (that contains additional mark-up) precisely by using the position taken from the raw content.\nI&#39;ll suggest a little hacky but effective alternative:\nCreate an overlay element looks like the one you are using to enter the code, and display the highlighted text on that. Hide the text on the first element so the user will see only highlighted &amp; overlayed content. Second element will have  so will be transparent to the mouse events. Only caret will be visible in the first element.\nPlease note that for this solution to work perfectly there must be nothing but the color difference between the rendered versions of highlighted and non-highlighted code.\nHere are the steps on how to do it:\n\nLet&#39;s call the first element \n\nCreate a second element named  that will have all the styles the first element has and place it on top of it (it must be next in the DOM).\n\nAdd some more styling to the first one:\n\n\n\n\nThis will hide the text while keeping the caret visible.\n\nAdd some more styling to the second one:\n\n\n\n\nThis will make the overlay element transparent for the caret underneath and also transparent to the mouse events.\n\nRun syntaxHighlighter on each keydown event fires on the first one\n\nAdjust scrollTop of the overlay element on each scroll event fires on the first\n\nsyntaxHighlighter will take the content from the first element and will set the content of the overlay\n\n\n\n","excerpt":"I can guess that it must be extremely hard to calculate the same caret position in highlighted content (that contains additional mark-up) precisely by using the position taken from the raw content.\nI&#39; &hellip; ","title":"On the web, how do you make the code be highlighted as the user is typing it? I only managed to make it that the code is highlighted on button click"},{"tags":["javascript","jquery","syntaxhighlighter"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":3,"is_answered":true,"question_id":27146783,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1685356170,"creation_date":1416997901,"body":"I use syntaxhighlighter in my page and it works well.\n\nBut it doesn&#39;t work when I save to a html file then use jquery load function to load them.\n\nEverything is displayed well except the code scope. Could some one tell me why? Thx!\n","excerpt":"I use syntaxhighlighter in my page and it works well.\n&lt;pre id=&quot;code&quot; class=&quot;brush:js&quot;&gt;\nsome code here\n&lt;/pre&gt;\n\nBut it doesn&#39;t work when I save to a html file then use jquery load function to load them. &hellip; ","title":"jQuery load() can not work with syntaxhighlighter"},{"tags":["python","swagger-ui","fastapi"],"question_score":4,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":76153626,"is_answered":false,"question_id":70034524,"item_type":"answer","score":4,"last_activity_date":1683020545,"creation_date":1683020545,"body":"I found out that one solution for this is to disable the syntax highlight in Swagger configurations. So I tried to deactivate it with FastAPI like this:\n\nAnd it&#39;s working now.\n","excerpt":"So I tried to deactivate it with FastAPI like this:\napp = FastAPI(\n        swagger_ui_parameters={&#39;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>&#39;: False}\n)\n\nAnd it&#39;s working now. &hellip; ","title":"Swagger ui RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded in FastAPI"},{"tags":["c++","arduino-esp32"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":4,"is_answered":true,"question_id":76149526,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1682987241,"creation_date":1682968258,"body":"I have a code with dozens of lines whose I wanted to compile with and without specific lines, as illustrated bellow:\n\nAnd I considered to have a macro to conditionally add a comment double-slash before the line in question, this way:\n\nThis is the macro definition:\n\nHowever, the problem is that, during compilation all the content right after double slashes // are considered as comments, including the &#39;}&#39; C++ statement. As you can see, even the syntaxhighlighter format it as comment.\nIs there any other approach to solve the issue ?\n","excerpt":"I have a code with dozens of lines whose I wanted to compile with and without specific lines, as illustrated bellow:\nx=1;\ny=2;  // I want to comment all &#39;y&#39; assignments on the code\nz=3;\n\nAnd I conside &hellip; ","title":"How to define a macro to conditionally &#39;comment&#39; specific code?"},{"tags":["javascript","html","reactjs"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":75922937,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1680550922,"creation_date":1680548647,"body":"I am getting a blog post html content as a string from a CMS using a REST API. I am using CK editor to write the post content. If I use a  tag in ck editor, it generates this HTML string.\n\nI am taking the above string and replacing the  tags with string  so that I can highlight the syntax in react. It is a custom tag used by react-syntax-highlighter library to highlight the syntax and I stored it in a string &quot;postContent&quot;. The string looks like this after the conversion.\n\nI pass this string to react Post component which then renders the HTML content.\n\nI have tried react-html-parser as well. Both of these methods, convert &quot;SyntaxHighlighter&quot; to &quot;syntaxhighlighter&quot; breaking the code.\nHow can I preserve the case, if not possible, are there any other methods to achieve my purpose?\n","excerpt":"I am getting a blog post html content as a string from a CMS using a REST API. I am using CK editor to write the post content. If I use a code tag in ck editor, it generates this HTML string.\n  &lt;pre&gt;\n &hellip; ","title":"Replace innerHtml with case sensitivity"},{"tags":["javascript","html","angular"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":75436499,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1676301286,"creation_date":1676294824,"body":"I am rendering json in pre tag through innerhtml in an angular application, Now it works perfectly fine but the render becomes slow and scrolling is also very slow when the json is huge. Is there a way to use concept of virtualisation and render only what is visible at a particular time? I know there&#39;s a module called ScrollingModule to do so but I am confused how to do it for innerHtml of a pre tag.\nMy html -&gt;\n\nWhere in syntaxHighlight function I am basically doing some editing of json to prettify it, which is -&gt;\n\nAny help would be appreciated, thankss :)\n","excerpt":"My html -&gt;\n           &lt;pre\n            [innerHTML]=&quot;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>()&quot;\n            class=&quot;pre-code&quot;\n            &gt;&lt;/pre&gt;\n\nWhere in <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> function I am basically doing some editing of json to prettify &hellip; it, which is -&gt;\n<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>() {\n        let json = JSON.stringify(this.jsonToBeRendered, undefined, 2);\n        // let json = this.jsonToBeRendered;\n        json = json.replace(/&amp;/g, &#39;&amp;amp;&#39;).replace &hellip; ","title":"How to use concept of virtualisation to render large json in innerHtml of pre tag in angular"},{"tags":["wordpress","markdown","syntaxhighlighter"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":75297090,"is_answered":false,"question_id":28798741,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1675167869,"creation_date":1675167869,"body":"Expanding on Pea3nut answer, I had to modify the PHP file for SyntaxHighlighter Evolved so it ended like this\nGo to Plugins -&gt; Plugin file editor -&gt; Select SyntaxHighlighter Evolved on the top right -&gt; Copy the gist in the link above -&gt; Select all and paste it there (replace it)\nThis also fixes the issue with Divi, so you don&#39;t have to pay for the Divi syntax highlighter code plugin and save $9 (it&#39;s free)\n","excerpt":"Expanding on Pea3nut answer, I had to modify the PHP file for SyntaxHighlighter Evolved so it ended like this\nGo to Plugins -&gt; Plugin file editor -&gt; Select SyntaxHighlighter Evolved on the top right - &hellip; ","title":"How to fix? Wordpress wp-markdown plugin corrupted syntax-highlighter-evolved plugin posts?"},{"tags":["swagger","swagger-ui"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":75223689,"is_answered":false,"question_id":43737575,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1674574247,"creation_date":1674574247,"body":"In FastAPI which uses Swagger UI, I was receiving the same error. I updated the FastAPI package to get the last version of Swagger UI and then set the value of &#39;syntaxHighlight&#39; to False, like below:\n\nJust search how you can set this param directly in Swagger UI. This may fix your issue.\n","excerpt":"I updated the FastAPI package to get the last version of Swagger UI and then set the value of &#39;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>&#39; to False, like below:\napp = FastAPI(swagger_ui_parameters={&#39;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>&#39;: False})\n\nJust &hellip; ","title":"Swagger-UI Maximum call stack size exceeded -&gt; Backreference"},{"tags":["formatting","blogs","blogger"],"question_score":296,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":1989915,"is_answered":false,"question_id":679189,"item_type":"answer","score":255,"last_activity_date":1671702882,"creation_date":1262385776,"body":"I&#39;ve created a blog post entry which explains how to add code syntax highlighting to blogger using the syntaxhighlighter 2.0\nHere&#39;s my blog post:\nhttp://www.craftyfella.com/2010/01/syntax-highlighting-with-blogger-engine.html\nI&#39;m quite impressed with what it can do.\nAbove Links stopped working.\nTry using http://hilite.me/\n","excerpt":"I&#39;ve created a blog post entry which explains how to add code syntax highlighting to blogger using the syntaxhighlighter 2.0\nHere&#39;s my blog post:\nhttp://www.craftyfella.com/2010/01/syntax-highlighting &hellip; ","title":"Formatting code snippets for blogging on Blogger"},{"tags":["flutter","gist","code-view"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":74877514,"is_answered":false,"question_id":74877358,"item_type":"answer","score":2,"last_activity_date":1671632830,"creation_date":1671632830,"body":"you can use syntax_highlighter package.\n\nTo display a block of code, use SyntaxHighlighter widget. You can specify the language of the code using the language parameter, and the actual code to be displayed using the text parameter. like example:\n\n","excerpt":"you can use syntax_highlighter package.\ndependencies:\n  syntax_highlighter: ^1.0.0\n\nimport &#39;package:syntax_highlighter/syntax_highlighter.dart&#39;;\n\nTo display a block of code, use SyntaxHighlighter widg &hellip; ","title":"how to display programming code as colorful and correctly formatted in flutter"},{"tags":["javascript","jquery","jquery-events"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":3282920,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1671470183,"creation_date":1279556586,"body":"I&#39;m trying to post-process content that is added to the DOM via the excellent SyntaxHighlighter project.\nWhen SH formats text, it generates a bunch of HTML and then writes that HTML into the DOM. It creates a div with class &quot;syntaxhighlighter&quot;.\nI want to listen for the insertion of these new divs, and when they are inserted, I want to manipulate some of the html and then overwrite the html in the DOM with this new html.\nMy problem is that when I write this new html back to the DOM, it re-triggers the event that fires my handler in the first place, and thus I get stuck in browser-killing recursion.\nHere&#39;s what I have so far:\n\nNeither the unbind nor the  nor the return false will get the behavior I want. I think I understand why, but I do not know how to stop it (my jQuery-foo is weak, I&#39;m afraid)\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m trying to post-process content that is added to the DOM via the excellent SyntaxHighlighter project.\nWhen SH formats text, it generates a bunch of HTML and then writes that HTML into the DOM. It c &hellip; ","title":"How would I stop a live jQuery event handler from firing more than once?"},{"tags":["c#",".net","regex","richtextbox","syntax-highlighting"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":3,"is_answered":true,"question_id":36734206,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1668443131,"creation_date":1461128446,"body":"I am writing a c# Html editor application, in which you type the code in a RichTextBox control. I want the RichTextBox to behave like notepad++ and other code editors in which the Html syntax gets highlighted in colors, like this for example:\n\n\n\nHow can I establish this in C# windows form RichTextBox? I have searched almost everywhere and didn&#39;t find anything that helped me. This is what I tried so far but I doesn&#39;t give the result I want:\n\n\n\nCan someone help me? What should I write inside the SyntaxHighlight() method? can someone give me the appropriate code?\nThank you\n","excerpt":"This is what I tried so far but I doesn&#39;t give the result I want:\n\nprivate void <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>()\n        {\n            string[] tags = { &quot;html&quot;,&quot;head&quot;,&quot;body&quot;,&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;,&quot;img&quot;,&quot;strong&quot;,&quot;p&quot;,&quot;h1&quot;,&quot;h2&quot;,&quot;h3&quot;, &hellip; What should I write inside the <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>() method? can someone give me the appropriate code?\nThank you &hellip; ","title":"How to highlight HTML syntax in C# windows form RichTextBox?"},{"tags":["c#",".net","regex","richtextbox","syntax-highlighting"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":74409072,"is_answered":false,"question_id":36734206,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1668443131,"creation_date":1668208448,"body":"A little late to the party but, after wanting to create my own offline version of CodePen, I implemented my own version of html syntax highlighting following CodePen&#39;s theme.\nThis does syntax highlighting and markup formatting, though the formatting depends on whether or not your html is well-formed.\nJust add this as a class for your RichTextBox, instantiate it accordingly and call it within whichever event works for you (I&#39;m using it with the RTB&#39;s double_click event but that does eliminate double-click text selection). What I&#39;m planning to do is add a timer, some boolean variables and work this within the key_up and key_down events to set the highlight update to be a bit more automatic and less intrusive on shortcuts. (which is hereby included below the class)\n\nHappy coding!\nEdit: I should also mention that !doctype breaks formatting as it&#39;s not exactly xml-friendly in the context of &quot;well-formed&quot;. For my purposes, all tags including body and relevant closings, css and js links are added programmatically at page save so only markup within the body tags are worked with inside the html RTB. This eliminates that problem.\nYou&#39;ll notice that this relies exclusively on Regex rather than on hard-coded tags and properties. I did this because tags and properties have a tendency to pop on and off the w3 scene quite often. That would force a dev to continually have to go back and edit those strings to remove deprecated tags / properties or to add new. Not optimal.\nI also thought it prudent to go ahead and include the instantiation / usage examples to make this a bit more plug&amp;play.\nAbove  public Main(), instantiate like so:\n\n... and, within your chosen event handler, call it like so:\n\nNaturally, adding a SaveFileDialog and an OpenFileDialog pretty much provides this the functionality of your very own, albeit very basic, html editor. Toss in a WebBrowser control and apply the RTB&#39;s text as the WebBrowser&#39;s source and you&#39;ve upgraded to live-view.\nIn the very least, this should serve as a viable reference for syntax highlighting in general. It really just boils down to identifying patterns and manipulating their colors so, for example, this will work effectively with css, javascript and even C# with some light adjusting of the pattern identification parameters.\nThe following is how I setup the automatic refresh with key_up / key_down and a timer set to 1000 ms:\n\n","excerpt":"Above  public Main(), instantiate like so:\n    #region Class Instantiation\n    <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span> syntax = new <span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>();\n    #endregion\n\n... and, within your chosen event handler, call it like so &hellip; ","title":"How to highlight HTML syntax in C# windows form RichTextBox?"},{"tags":["swagger-ui","springdoc"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":74328555,"is_answered":false,"question_id":74226603,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1667658320,"creation_date":1667658320,"body":"The settings in application.yaml are correct.\nI think it&#39;s probably because I&#39;m using cache for js files.\nFor example, you can check what is not cached by accessing with the following URL.\n\n\nTry doing a hard refresh in your browser.\n","excerpt":"deepLinking: true,\n     <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>: {activated: false},\npresets: [\n...\n\nTry doing a hard refresh in your browser. &hellip; ","title":"How to disable Swagger UI syntax highlighting in Springdoc?"},{"tags":["javascript","ace-editor"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":74209409,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1666813516,"creation_date":1666794293,"body":"I have a page containing multiple instances of ace.js editors, all on read-only, displaying code.\n\nI wish to open the editor like so and highlight its content to allow my user to easily copy it, like so:\n\nMy current approach does not show the wanted result, it does open an editor with the code inside of it BUT its height is not at the size of its content:\n\nHeres&#39;s how I do it:\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\nDoes anyone of you have recommendations or perhaps my approach is faulty?\nThank you !\n\n","excerpt":"/mode/${language}`,\n      theme: &#39;ace/theme/monokai&#39;,\n      startLineNumber: 1,\n      trim: true,\n    });\n  });\n}\n\n// STARTS HERE\n// Called on page load to highlight each block of code\nfunction <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"Open Ace.js code editor and select content on click"},{"tags":["swagger","swagger-ui","openapi","quarkus","openapi-generator"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":73984320,"item_type":"question","score":3,"last_activity_date":1665134315,"creation_date":1665130767,"body":"I am developing a Rest-API service using  and for this, I have added   (org.eclipse.microprofile.openapi) annotations to generate . My response can consist of large amounts of data, so I have used the  (from SmallRye Mutiny) so as to return the response asynchronously during execution.\nEverything works perfectly when a small set of data is returned to , The problem arises when a large set of data is returned to Swagger-UI then I believe the Swagger-UI waits for the complete response and the browser stops responding and crashes.\nHowever, when I make a request to the same API endpoint using the  command, I see that  is working perfectly and returning the response asynchronously and displaying it on the command line, so nothing breaks in  command and everything works perfectly here, even for very large sets of returned data.\nIs there something that I can do so as to avoid the crashing of Swagger-UI, like some additional  annotation or some custom classes, so as to avoid the Swagger-UI waiting and displaying the results as and when they are received?\nUpdated things I have tried the following based on other answers:\n\nI found that some answers have mentioned disabling the  so I tried the same by adding the following lines in my  but it is still not working and swagger-ui hangs:\n\n\n","excerpt":"Updated things I have tried the following based on other answers:\n\nI found that some answers have mentioned disabling the <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> so I tried the same by adding the following lines in my application.yml &hellip; but it is still not working and swagger-ui hangs:\n\nquarkus:\n  swagger-ui:\n    always-include: true\n    <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span>:\n      activated: false\n  http:\n    cors: true\n    port: 8080 &hellip; ","title":"How to configure Swagger-UI to display results as and when received asynchronously instead of waiting for the complete results?"},{"tags":["javascript","regex"],"question_score":-1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":57451326,"item_type":"question","score":-1,"last_activity_date":1664926800,"creation_date":1565537557,"body":"Bascom uses a special format to comment out blocks of code. I want a RegEx that matches this block to be used in SyntaxHighlighter.\n\nThese comment blocks starts with &#39;( and ends with &#39;).\nYep, it&#39;s so stupid.\n\nExample input:\n\n\n\nI tried:\n    &#39;\\(.*?\\)&#39;\nand many others without success.\n\nExpected return after replace:\n\n\n\nwhere ##### is the replacement.\n\nBasically just like C++ &amp; similar /* .. */ rule. But I can&#39;t get it working.\n\nThanks in advance!\n","excerpt":"Bascom uses a special format to comment out blocks of code. I want a RegEx that matches this block to be used in SyntaxHighlighter.\n\nThese comment blocks starts with &#39;( and ends with &#39;).\nYep, it&#39;s so  &hellip; ","title":"Match for custom comment block required"},{"tags":["javascript","json","angular","workflow","mxgraph"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":73885312,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1664397692,"creation_date":1664384551,"body":"I am trying to work with Angular and MX Graphs using JSON, I am sure that many of you also would think it is a great way to serialize graphs and also give them functionality within an angular application.\nI have not been able to find a minimum example where a JSON representation of a graph is rendered from Angular.\nInn the demo part of this example with mxgraph using javascript, they simply render the graph from a json structure.\nExample:\nhttps://codepen.io/Gatcha/pen/oYexEB\nJSON Structure\n\nand this is the Javascript code that renders the graph, where the json is obtained from a text area called &quot;from&quot; and pased to JSON, pretty basic and simple:\n\nDoes anyone have a little Idea of how to do this with Angular, in any way in order to start documenting this for everyone also?\nThanks a lot.\nMay the force be with you.\nNote: There is the mxHierarchicalLayout.js class that i think would allow you to create a hierarchical model of the graph.\nHere is the whole javascript file.\nI will keep trying and post whatever I learn, but please if you have a hint, would be really apretiated.\n\n","excerpt":"dataModel);\n}));\n\ndocument.getElementById(&#39;buttons&#39;).appendChild(mxUtils.button(&#39;To JSON&#39;, () =&gt; {\n  const jsonNodes = graphX.getJsonModel();\n  document.getElementById(&#39;to&#39;).innerHTML = `&lt;pre&gt;${<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; dataModel);\n}));\n\ndocument.getElementById(&#39;buttons&#39;).appendChild(mxUtils.button(&#39;To JSON&#39;, () =&gt; {\n  const jsonNodes = graphX.getJsonModel();\n  document.getElementById(&#39;to&#39;).innerHTML = `&lt;pre&gt;${<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"MXGraph JSON Graphs with Angular - render and read graph using JSON and ANGULAR with mxGraph"},{"tags":["c#",".net","asp.net","blogengine.net"],"question_score":3,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":4,"is_answered":true,"question_id":3191999,"item_type":"question","score":3,"last_activity_date":1659600027,"creation_date":1278478127,"body":"I&#39;m testing a Tiny_MCE plugin for BlogEngine.NET extension I wrote earlier and I keep receiving the following error message whenever I use my own extension or the extremely popular SyntaxHighlighter extension which both have similar behaviors and both implement Tiny_MCE plugins:\n\nUrl :\n&#39;http://localhost/admin/Pages/Add_entry.aspx&#39;\nRaw Url : /admin/Pages/Add_entry.aspx\nMessage : A potentially dangerous\nRequest.Form value was detected from\nthe client\n(ctl00$cphAdmin$txtContent$TinyMCE1$txtContent=&quot;\nSource : System.WebStackTrace :    at\nSystem.Web.HttpRequest.ValidateString(String\nvalue, String collectionKey,\nRequestValidationSource\nrequestCollection)   at\nSystem.Web.HttpRequest.ValidateNameValueCollection(NameValueCollection\nnvc, RequestValidationSource\nrequestCollection)   at\nSystem.Web.HttpRequest.get_Form()   at\nSystem.Web.HttpRequest.get_Item(String\nkey)   at\nBlogEngine.Core.Web.HttpModules.CompressionModule.context_PostReleaseRequestState(Object\nsender, EventArgs e) in\nD:\\Projects\\Be-1610\\BlogEngine\\DotNetSlave.BusinessLogic\\Web\\HttpModules\\CompressionModule.cs:line\n62   at\nSystem.Web.HttpApplication.SyncEventExecutionStep.System.Web.HttpApplication.IExecutionStep.Execute()\nat\nSystem.Web.HttpApplication.ExecuteStep(IExecutionStep\nstep, Boolean&amp;\ncompletedSynchronously)TargetSite :\nVoid ValidateString(System.String,\nSystem.String,\nSystem.Web.Util.RequestValidationSource)\n\nMy question is thus: although I receive this error on my local environment (IIS 7.5 ASP.NET 4.0 Integrated App Pool) I receive no error whatsoever on my live environment (IIS 7.5 ASP.NET 3.5 SP1/ 3.0 / 2.0.) Additionally whenever I test the extension using debug mode in Visual Studio 2010 and run the site off of a separate instance I don&#39;t receive this error.\nI&#39;m almost certain that the fact that this issue only occurs on my localhost IIS instance indicates that it&#39;s a configuration issue or a behavior specific to ASP.NET 4.0, but I don&#39;t know what exactly. Do any of you know what might be causing this?\n","excerpt":"I&#39;m testing a Tiny_MCE plugin for BlogEngine.NET extension I wrote earlier and I keep receiving the following error message whenever I use my own extension or the extremely popular SyntaxHighlighter e &hellip; ","title":"Are conditions for raising &quot;potentially dangerous Request.Form value&quot; errors dependent on .NET configuration and version?"},{"tags":["php","mediawiki"],"question_score":0,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":0,"is_answered":false,"question_id":73087935,"item_type":"question","score":0,"last_activity_date":1658548867,"creation_date":1658548867,"body":"I was using syntaxhighlight plugin for rendering my code.\nI design a template for it and afer that I create a form base on it.\nThe template is this, where I just want to pass parameters code and type:\n\nThe problem is that when code contains the pipe symbol (&#39;|&#39;) things will go wrong.\nI&#39;m seeking any way to making code a pure text variable to make it work.\n","excerpt":"I was using <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> plugin for rendering my code.\nI design a template for it and afer that I create a form base on it. &hellip; ","title":"How to pass parameters as TEXT in mediawiki"},{"tags":["wiki","mediawiki-extensions","wikimedia"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":42442211,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1657358866,"creation_date":1487949627,"body":"I would like to use Template parameters within syntaxhighlight. For instance, something like:\n\n\n\nWhere  and  are the template parameters to be replaced. The content is multiline and may contain pipe characters, etc.\n","excerpt":"I would like to use Template parameters within <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>. &hellip; For instance, something like:\n\n &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> lang=&quot;scala&quot;&gt;\n val x: Boolean = {{{xVal}}}\n val y: Boolean = {{{yVal}}} | x\n &lt;/<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>&gt;\n\n\nWhere xVal and yVal are the template parameters to be &hellip; ","title":"How to use template parameters in wiki syntaxhighlight?"},{"tags":["css","syntax-highlighting","syntaxhighlighter"],"question_score":2,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":2,"is_answered":true,"question_id":21109408,"item_type":"question","score":2,"last_activity_date":1657150712,"creation_date":1389689978,"body":"I am using Syntax Highlighter for my website.But how can I use it for inline code? I  mean when I use it for inline code it still shows the line number  and I want to remove it as it makes no sense to show line number for inline code\n\ni.e\n\nI want\n\n&quot;This is a java print code &quot;\n\ninstead of\n\n&quot;This is a java print code &quot; \n\n(notice the line number in second case)\n\nI searched it on google but no success.\n","excerpt":"I am using Syntax Highlighter for my website.But how can I use it for inline code? I  mean when I use it for inline code it still shows the line number 1 and I want to remove it as it makes no sense t &hellip; ","title":"How to use SyntaxHighlighter for inline code"},{"tags":["javascript","regex","syntax-highlighting","confluence","brush"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":34589901,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1655473742,"creation_date":1451906177,"body":"I tried to write a custom code macro syntax for a language that uses semicolon as a comment character. \n\nThis shows how to do this:\nhttp://alexgorbatchev.com/SyntaxHighlighter/manual/brushes/\n\nMy regex looks like this:\n\n\n\nBut this not only makes the line with the semicolon green, it also does funny things to other lines:\n\n becomes  (Note: it added a semicolon after the right angle bracket!) where everything behind the semicolon is green!\n\nWhy is this? How ist the right syntax for comments with semicolons?\n","excerpt":"I tried to write a custom code macro syntax for a language that uses semicolon as a comment character. \n\nThis shows how to do this:\nhttp://alexgorbatchev.com/SyntaxHighlighter/manual/brushes/\n\nMy rege &hellip; ","title":"Atlassian Confluence: custom code macro - semicolon in brush syntax causes error"},{"tags":["mediawiki","syntax-highlighting"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":72111831,"is_answered":false,"question_id":57515213,"item_type":"answer","score":1,"last_activity_date":1651661803,"creation_date":1651661803,"body":"That is because syntaxhighlight in &gt;MediaWiki 1.31 requires Python.\n[https://www.mediawiki.org/wiki/Extension:SyntaxHighlight#Installation][1]\nBesides I am looking for how to install python in a2hosted.\n","excerpt":"That is because <span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> in &gt;MediaWiki 1.31 requires Python. &hellip; ","title":"How to enable the SyntaxHighlight extension after installed?"},{"tags":["mediawiki","syntax-highlighting"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":false,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":true,"question_id":57515213,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1651661803,"creation_date":1565897819,"body":"I have a fresh Mediawiki (v1.33) installed into fresh UBUNTU 18 LTS... The &#39;&#39;SyntaxHighlight&#39;&#39; extension is not working, the effect is like a code into  tags.\n\nAt mediawiki.org/list there are no clues. I used the syntax_highlighting checkbox during Mediawiki installation, and I can see it at  page as &quot;SyntaxHighlight   2.0&quot;, so, it is installed... But is not working. \n\n\n\nNOTES AND TESTS\n\nNotes. \n\n\nIt is a corporative Wiki, no way to offer public URL... But it is a fresh, standard and controlled installation, all reproductive and standard.\nThe Wiki was configured with skin &quot;Vector&quot; and language &quot;Brazilian Portuguese&quot;. \n\n\nTests.\n\n\nUsage tests of mediawiki.org/Extension:SyntaxHighlight, the Python example.\n\n1.1. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\n\n1.2. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\nPHP example, fragment from wikipedia.org/PHP Syntax.\n\n2.1. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\n\n2.2. With tag . Result: no highlight, same as .\n\n\nThe code fragments used in the tests:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNOTE2: IT IS NOT A DUPLICATE\n\nThis question is similar but not same as this other one: here is about the basic &quot;Hello World&quot; of the extension, for any , and the other is about an specific  installation. We need to solver first here, them, solve the other.\n","excerpt":"The &#39;&#39;<span class=\"highlight\">SyntaxHighlight</span>&#39;&#39; extension is not working, the effect is like a code into &lt;pre&gt; tags.\n\nAt mediawiki.org/list there are no clues. &hellip; With tag &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>&gt;. Result: no highlight, same as &lt;pre&gt;.\n\n2.2. With tag &lt;source&gt;. Result: no highlight, same as &lt;pre&gt;. &hellip; ","title":"How to enable the SyntaxHighlight extension after installed?"},{"tags":["mediawiki"],"question_score":-2,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":72022541,"is_answered":false,"question_id":72020650,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1651025763,"creation_date":1651025763,"body":"Activate SyntaxHighlight in your  with . make sure  has execution permissions and wrap your code snippets with ,\nOR\nwrap your snippets with ,\nOR\nindent every line of your snippets with at least one space.\n","excerpt":"wrap your code snippets with &lt;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span> lang=&quot;C++&quot;&gt;... &hellip; &lt;/<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxhighlight</span>&gt;,\nOR\nwrap your snippets with &lt;pre&gt;...&lt;/pre&gt;,\nOR\nindent every line of your snippets with at least one space. &hellip; ","title":"MediaWiki breaks when I put C++ code in preformatted text"},{"tags":["javascript","html"],"question_score":8,"is_accepted":false,"answer_id":71283819,"is_answered":false,"question_id":41884969,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1645956373,"creation_date":1645956373,"body":"You can&#39;t have syntax highlighting in a contenteditable div, because the colors will get mixed up. But you can make a contenteditable div AND a normal div which will show the colors and place them in the same position. (Believe me, there are no external js files. See the code below.)\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\n","excerpt":"syncScroll(element1, element2) {\nelement2.scrollLeft = element1.scrollLeft;\nelement2.scrollTop = element1.scrollTop;\n}\n\nwindow.onload = function() {\nvar code = document.getElementById(&quot;code&quot;);\n<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; 15px;\noverflow: auto;\nwidth: 500px;\nheight: 500px;\nborder: 1px solid black;\nword-wrap: break-word;\n}\n\n#colorCode {\nuser-select: none;\n}\r\n&lt;div&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;colorCode&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;code&quot; oninput=&quot;<span class=\"highlight\">syntaxHighlight</span> &hellip; ","title":"Highlight syntax in contenteditable"},{"tags":["qt","cmake","qtquick2","webassembly","conan"],"question_score":1,"is_accepted":false,"has_accepted_answer":true,"answer_count":1,"is_answered":false,"question_id":70961446,"item_type":"question","score":1,"last_activity_date":1644409470,"creation_date":1643829003,"body":"I have a really simple Qt (QML) project :\nCMakeLists.txt :\n\nconanfile.txt :\n\nmain.cpp :\n\nmain.qml :\n\nqml.qrc :\n\nAs you can see, it is downloading the official Qt conan packages, from the Qt conan server. (So it does NOT use the conan packages from the conan-center-index server.)\nI can successfully build and run it under my macOS machine using this script :\nbuild_and_run.sh :\n\nI am trying to build it for WebAssembly as well, using this script :\nbuildWasm.sh :\n\nThe build fails with this error :\n\n...and indeed : QtQuick is in the qtdeclarative conan folder (/Users/myUser/.conan/data/qtbase/6.2.2/qt/everywhere/package/...), and not in the qtbase folder.\nHow could I fix this issue?\nI am following these documentation pages :\nhttps://www.qt.io/blog/installing-qt-via-conan-package-manager\nhttps://wiki.qt.io/Using_Conan_for_Qt6\nhttps://www.qt.io/blog/qt-6-build-system\nTo simplify things : my project can be downloaded from here as well (every sources that I shared above) :\nhttps://wetransfer.com/downloads/e8717b634b2eff069134b4407f77243c20220202190736/81e9433c52a22081915a7d5d144e2ef420220202190748/a8ec17\nUPDATE :\nI just tried this widget application : Qt/Examples/Qt-6.2.1/widgets/richtext/syntaxhighlighter/ .\nIt works well, using the exact same  and  that I shared above.\nHere is a screenshot as well about this Example application, that I compiled for WebAssembly, running in Chrome :\n\nSo it seems like that the issue is with the QtQuick module...\nPossible solution ideas are very well welcomed!\nI tried many things, but nothing worked so far...\n","excerpt":"I have a really simple Qt (QML) project :\nCMakeLists.txt :\ncmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.12.2)\n\nproject(testtttt VERSION 0.1 LANGUAGES CXX)\n\nset(CMAKE_INCLUDE_CURRENT_DIR ON)\n\nset(CMAKE_AUTOUIC ON) &hellip; ","title":"Qt Webassembly via conan package manager"},{"tags":["javascript","html","css","wordpress"],"question_score":-1,"is_accepted":true,"answer_id":70797302,"is_answered":false,"question_id":70752444,"item_type":"answer","score":0,"last_activity_date":1642746937,"creation_date":1642746937,"body":"These are the following methods:\n\nYou may use the plugin &quot;Header and Footer&quot; (This plugin have different TABS like html, CSS, JavaScript) and add your whole in this plugin. So Your code work in whole WordPress website.\nFirst, you need to install and activate the SyntaxHighlighter Evolved plugin. For more details, see our step by step guide on how to install a WordPress plugin.\nUpon activation, you can go ahead and edit the blog post where you want to display the code.\n\n","excerpt":"These are the following methods:\n\nYou may use the plugin &quot;Header and Footer&quot; (This plugin have different TABS like html, CSS, JavaScript) and add your whole in this plugin. So Your code work in whole  &hellip; ","title":"Adding external HTML CSS and Javascript in Wordpress"}],"has_more":true,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":254}